@Mohammad in that case there is no need for the summation :-). So in the case of just one function, as you imply, yes, we take the squared $c_i$ outside the integral (because it is a constant):
$$\\int \\varphi(\\xi)(c_1G^1(\\xi))^2d\\xi=c_1^2\\int \\varphi(\\xi)(G^1(\\xi))^2d\\xi.$$

About the small-o notation in this particular book (which I interpreted as the same as the big-O notation), you can see more here: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Big_O_notation.

