Thanks so much @Bill. I am going to work on this. Just one more question, Is there a reason to use $Q^{-1}$ instead of $\\left(\\frac{X'X}{N}\\right)^{-1}$? The latter seams reasonable, and avoids the issue of calculating the probability limit. It would be \\begin{align}
\\tilde{\\beta} = \\left(I-\\left(\\frac{X'X}{N}\\right)^{-1}D_{\\eta\\eta} \\right)^{-1}\\left(\\hat{\\beta}_{OLS} - \\left(\\frac{X'X}{N}\\right)^{-1}D_{\\eta\\epsilon} \\right)
\\end{align}

