@Alexis: According to wikipedia ` The probability density function of the Laplace distribution is also reminiscent of the normal distribution
; however, whereas the normal distribution is expressed in terms of the squared difference from the mean μ, the Laplace density is expressed in terms of theabsolute difference
 from the mean. Consequently the Laplace distribution has fatter tails than the normal distribution`
